Serve privacy policy from the app site instead of a /docs Pages source

The site is deployed by the GitHub Actions workflow from dist/, so publishing
the policy out of /docs required switching the Pages source away from Actions
- which took the site down with a 404.

Move the page to public/privacy/index.html so it builds into dist/ and ships
with the app at /privacy/, keeping Actions as the Pages source. Also add a
workbox navigateFallbackDenylist for /privacy so the service worker doesn't
serve the SPA shell in place of the static page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
